WEBVTT

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:16.550
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>From WBEZ Chicago, it's This American Life. I'm Chana Joffe-Walt, sitting in for Ira Glass. This all started with a phone call, a call that eventually led to this episode. So that's where I'm going to start. I was talking to a journalist in Gaza on the phone.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>这里是芝加哥 WBEZ 电台的《美国生活》。我是 Chana Joffe-Walt，代替 Ira Glass 主持节目。这一切始于一通电话，正是这通电话促成了这期节目。所以，我想从这里开始讲起。我当时正在和加沙的一位记者通话。

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:17.060
<v Maram Hamaid>Hello?
<v Maram Hamaid>喂？

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.210
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Hi, this is Chana. Hi.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你好，我是 Chana。你好。

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:20.310
<v Maram Hamaid>How are you?
<v Maram Hamaid>你好吗？

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:41.760
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>This was back in April. I'd been speaking to people in Gaza for months by then, but nobody where Maram was, in the middle area, Deir Balah. Maram Hamaid, she's a reporter for Al Jazeera English. We were chatting. I was asking some pretty basic questions about what she was experiencing, what she was seeing, what the day had been like. She got interrupted.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>那是四月份的事。到那时为止，我已经和加沙的人们交谈了几个月，但没人像 Maram 那样住在加沙中部代尔拜拉赫（Deir Balah）。Maram Hamaid 是半岛电视台英语频道的记者。我们当时在聊天。我问了一些关于她的经历、所见所闻以及一天过得如何的基础问题。她被中途打断了。

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:47.420
<v Maram Hamaid>It was a little bit calm day in Deir Balah. You know, like--
<v Maram Hamaid>代尔拜拉赫今天还算平静。你知道，就像——

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:48.920
<v Banias>Who is it, Mom?
<v Banias>妈妈，是谁呀？

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:52.740
<v Maram Hamaid>So Banias is listening. I need to introduce Banias to you.
<v Maram Hamaid>Banias 正在听。我得给你介绍一下 Banias。

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:53.930
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Hi, Banias.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你好，Banias。

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:54.410
<v Banias>Hi.
<v Banias>你好。

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:56.510
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>How are you?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你好吗？

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:58.560
<v Banias>I'm fine, thank you.
<v Banias>我很好，谢谢。

00:00:58.560 --> 00:00:59.400
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Good.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>很好。

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:02.650
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Maram and I kept talking-- or trying to.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我和 Maram 继续交谈——或者说尝试交谈。

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:04.870
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And you're in Deir Balah? Are you in Deir Balah?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你是在代尔拜拉赫吗？你现在在代尔拜拉赫吗？

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:05.550
<v Banias>Now what do I do?
<v Banias>现在我该怎么办？

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:06.610
<v Maram Hamaid>Yeah, we are in Deir Balah--
<v Maram Hamaid>是啊，我们在代尔拜拉赫——

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:06.990
<v Banias>Mom--
<v Banias>妈妈——

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:08.500
<v Maram Hamaid>--in the central area.
<v Maram Hamaid>——在中部地区。

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:11.280
<v Banias>--now what do I do?
<v Banias>——现在我该怎么办？

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.600
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Is that where you're from? Is that where your home is, or did you--
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>那是你的家乡吗？你是住在自己家，还是……

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:18.330
<v Maram Hamaid>Uh, no. I'm displaced.
<v Maram Hamaid>呃，不。我是流离失所者。

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:18.900
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yeah.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>是啊。

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:28.350
<v Maram Hamaid>And we're living in our relative's home here, with around 80 other family members.
<v Maram Hamaid>我们住在这里的亲戚家里，和大约 80 位家庭成员挤在一起。

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:29.010
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Wow.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>天哪。

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:30.240
<v Banias>"Ay-dee"!
<v Banias>“Ay-dee”！

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:30.840
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yeah.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>是啊。

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:34.390
<v Banias>It's "ay-dee," not "ay-tee." Not "ay-tee."
<v Banias>是“Ay-dee”，不是“Ay-tee”。不是“Ay-tee”。

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:35.650
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>That's a lot of people.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>那人可真多。

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:38.260
<v Maram Hamaid>Yeah. Yeah, yeah. Like a big number--
<v Maram Hamaid>是啊，是啊，是啊。人数非常多——

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:39.880
<v Banias>Mom, it's "ay-dee," not "ay-tee."
<v Banias>妈妈，是“Ay-dee”，不是“Ay-tee”。

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:48.420
<v Maram Hamaid>So Banias is correcting me regarding the American accent, OK? So she's saying, like, what is it? It's "ay-tee" or "ay-dee"?
<v Maram Hamaid>所以 Banias 正在纠正我的美国口音，对吧？她是在说……是哪个词？是“Ay-tee”还是“Ay-dee”？

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:49.290
<v Banias>"Ay-dee"!
<v Banias>“Ay-dee”！

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:49.590
<v Maram Hamaid>Oh.
<v Maram Hamaid>哦。

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:51.060
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>"Ay-dee." "Ay-dee."
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>“Ay-dee”。“Ay-dee”。

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:52.620
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Does she correct you a lot?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她经常纠正你吗？

00:01:52.620 --> 00:02:01.480
<v Maram Hamaid>Yeah! A lot, a lot. She speaks English better than me because I started with her from very young.
<v Maram Hamaid>会！经常，经常。她的英语比我好，因为她很小的时候我就开始教她了。

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:01.800
<v Banias>Back to me.
<v Banias>回到我这里。

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.230
<v Maram Hamaid>I'm here around Banias--
<v Maram Hamaid>我在这里陪着 Banias——

00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:04.710
<v Banias>Back to me.
<v Banias>回到我这里。

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:07.550
<v Maram Hamaid>Back to me. [LAUGHS] Yeah.
<v Maram Hamaid>回到我这里。[笑] 是的。

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:09.710
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And where--
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>那——

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:11.060
<v Maram Hamaid>She's-- yeah.
<v Maram Hamaid>她是——是的。

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:13.130
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Does she want to talk?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她想说话吗？

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:13.460
<v Maram Hamaid>Yeah.
<v Maram Hamaid>想的。

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:18.230
<v Banias>Yeah, I'm pretty ready. I'm ready, ready.
<v Banias>是的，我已经准备好了。我准备好了，真的准备好了。

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:21.980
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>You're ready, ready. How old are you, Banias?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你准备好了，真的准备好了。Banias，你几岁了？

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:24.090
<v Banias>I'm eight years old.
<v Banias>我今年八岁。

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:28.430
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>You're eight years old. And where did you learn to speak like an American?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你今年八岁。你是从哪里学会像美国人那样说话的？

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:29.880
<v Banias>From Mama.
<v Banias>从妈妈那里。

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:32.790
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Uh-huh. She speaks to you in English?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>嗯哼。她用英语和你交流吗？

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:37.770
<v Banias>Yeah. Do you hear that? Do you hear that wee-wee-wee?
<v Banias>是啊。你听到了吗？你听到那个呼呼呼的声音了吗？

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:39.680
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>I do. Yeah. What is it?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>听到了。是的，那是什么？

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:42.900
<v Maram Hamaid>So Banias is-- [SIGHS] what is it?
<v Maram Hamaid>Banias 正——[叹气] 那是什么？

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:46.320
<v Banias>It's the whoosh, whoosh, whoosh. A war plane.
<v Banias>那是呼啸声，呼啸声，呼啸声。是战机。

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:50.030
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>It's a warplane. I do hear it, yeah.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>是战机。我确实听到了，是的。

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:55.490
<v Banias>I, of course, hear it, because it never ends.
<v Banias>我当然听得见，因为它从没停过。

00:02:55.490 --> 00:03:16.410
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Banias then takes the phone from her mom-- having told me what they are hearing, begins pointing out what they're seeing, saying, look at this-- as if I can also see, even though we're not on a video call. She says, here we have the window, as you can see. Here's the curtains. There are flowers. We don't have any sofas, just-- Mom, how do you say it?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Banias 随后从她妈妈手中接过电话——在告诉我他们听到了什么之后，她开始指出他们所看到的一切，说，看这个——就好像我也能看到一样，尽管我们并没有在进行视频通话。她说，正如你所见，这里有窗户。这里是窗帘。那里有花。我们没有任何沙发，只有——妈妈，那个词怎么说？

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:17.670
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Mattresses?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>床垫？

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:32.520
<v Banias>Just "may-tresses," as you can see. We sit sometimes on bed, on the ground. Women are covering their heads all the time, as you can see.
<v Banias>正如你所见，只有“床垫”。我们有时坐在床上，有时坐在地上。正如你所见，女人们一直用头巾遮住头。

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:36.130
<v Maram Hamaid>[LAUGHS] She couldn't see. You should tell her.
<v Maram Hamaid>[笑] 她看不到的。你应该告诉她。

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:37.060
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yeah, tell me.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>是啊，告诉我吧。

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:40.450
<v Banias>OK. Oh, did you see our room?
<v Banias>好的。哦，你看到我们的房间了吗？

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:40.950
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>No.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>没有。

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:48.630
<v Banias>If you see it, you will-- you will run, run, run, run from this.
<v Banias>如果你看到它，你肯定会——你肯定会从这里逃跑，跑啊跑啊跑啊。

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:48.930
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Why?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>为什么？

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:49.500
<v Maram Hamaid>[LAUGHS]
<v Maram Hamaid>[笑]

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:53.680
<v Banias>Because it's so old and dusty.
<v Banias>因为它太老旧、太脏了。

00:03:53.680 --> 00:04:11.740
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Maram told me later she was so surprised at Banias's performance in this call. That was the word she used. Apparently, Banias was marching around with the phone in front of her, telling people, I need the room, please, jumping on the mattress, standing on the table, pointing, saying, here's my brother, Iyas.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Maram 后来告诉我，她对 Banias 在这次通话中的表现感到非常惊讶。这就是她用的词。显然，Banias 拿着手机在她面前走来走去，对周围的人说，请给我留点空间，在床垫上跳来跳去，站在桌子上，指着说，这是我的弟弟 Iyas。

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:16.750
<v Banias>There he is. He's pretty and smart like me.
<v Banias>看，那就是他。他和一样我漂亮聪明。

00:04:16.750 --> 00:05:02.720
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Gaza is full of kids. About half the population is under 18 years old, and about half of that group is under 10 years old, like Banias. A huge way in which children in this war are different from kids in other war zones is that children in Gaza are not allowed to leave. They're not displaced to some other spot away from the fighting. They're displaced inside Gaza. They're stuck in the violence and stuck with their families, in crowded rooms or tents, doing the things that kids everywhere do, building their inner world, trying to make sense of the world around them. I was calling Maram that day to ask about the situation in Deir Balah, and Banias took the phone and said, no, no, no, don't ask her. Ask me.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>加沙到处都是孩子。大约一半的人口在 18 岁以下，而其中约一半在 10 岁以下，就像 Banias 一样。这场战争中的孩子们与其他战区的孩子最大的不同在于，加沙的孩子们不被允许离开。他们并没有被转移到远离战火的其他地方，而是被困在加沙内部。他们被困在暴力之中，与家人挤在狭窄的房间或帐篷里，做着世界各地孩子都会做的事——建立自己的内心世界，试图理解周围的世界。那天我打电话给 Maram 询问代尔拜拉赫的情况，Banias 抢过电话说，不，不，不，不要问她。问我。

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:06.470
<v Banias>Being in Deir a Balah is boring.
<v Banias>待在代尔拜拉赫很无聊。

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:08.060
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>It's boring?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>很无聊吗？

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:10.260
<v Banias>Really boring.
<v Banias>非常无聊。

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:10.710
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yeah.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>是啊。

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:29.280
<v Banias>Not just-- bored, so bored. I really miss the burgers. And now we are on canned food. We have just the boxes of food, the food boxes. One day-- I want to tell you something.
<v Banias>不仅仅是……无聊，太无聊了。我真的很想念汉堡。现在我们只能吃罐头食品。我们只有食品盒，那些食品盒。有一天——我想告诉你一件事。

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:30.500
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Tell me.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>告诉我。

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:59.940
<v Banias>One day, when we are sitting in our room talking about something, then boom! A big bomb broke all of the windows, and the home was shaking. And my baby brother, Iyas, has got injured in his head. We have noticed the glass in his head.
<v Banias>有一天，当我们坐在房间里聊天时，突然“砰”的一声！一颗巨大的炸弹震碎了所有的窗户，房子都在摇晃。我的弟弟 Iyas 的头部受伤了。我们注意到他头上有玻璃碎片。

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:03.460
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Oof. Is he OK, Banias?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>天哪。他没事吧，Banias？

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:07.360
<v Banias>Yes, now he's all right.
<v Banias>是的，他现在没事了。

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:16.300
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>We talked for a while and then said goodbye. That was the end of April. And then, in July, I saw Maram's name on my phone.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我们聊了一会儿便说了再见。那是四月底。到了七月，我在手机上看到了 Maram 的名字。

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:24.110
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Hi. Maram? Can you hear me? Hello?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>喂？Maram？你能听到吗？喂？

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:24.880
<v Banias>Yeah.
<v Banias>在呢。

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:31.210
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>It was Banias. She wanted to talk, tell me about her day. Then, another day.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>是 Banias。她想和我聊天，告诉我她的一天。然后，又过了几天。

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:32.230
<v Banias>Hello.
<v Banias>喂。

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:33.610
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Hi, Banias.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你好，Banias。

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:34.940
<v Banias>Do you want to talk to me?
<v Banias>你想和我聊天吗？

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:37.210
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yeah, sure. What are you doing?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>当然。你在做什么？

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:56.850
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Through the summer, into the fall, Banias called me, and I called her. Maram, her mother, gave permission for these phone calls, but it was always just Banias on the line, telling me about herself and her life. I wanted to know what it's like to be a kid in this war. And here was this kid who wanted to talk.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>整个夏天，一直到秋天，Banias 不时打电话给我，我也打给她。她的母亲 Maram 允许进行这些通话，但每次线上都只有 Banias，向我诉说关于她自己和生活的一切。我想知道作为一个孩子身处这场战争中是什么感觉。而这里有一个渴望交流的孩子。

00:06:56.850 --> 00:07:09.660
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Banias was a natural narrator of her own life. She was constantly directing my attention. These are my friends. This is my school stationery, as you can see. Do you want to know what we're doing right now? I'll tell you.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Banias 是自己生活的天生叙述者。她不断引导我的注意力。这是我的朋友们。正如你所见，这是我的学校文具。你想知道我们现在在做什么吗？我告诉你。

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:27.690
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Unfortunately for me, she also had zero interest in satisfying my journalistic agenda. If I asked Banias a question she was not interested in, she'd yawn dramatically, stage yawn. [YAWNS] It's getting late. I'm so tired. Let's look over here.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>不幸的是，她对我那些所谓的新闻访谈议程毫无兴趣。如果我问了 Banias 一个她不感兴趣的问题，她会夸张地打哈欠。[打哈欠] 天色晚了。我好累。我们看那边吧。

00:07:27.690 --> 00:07:40.530
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>I had been reading and thinking about what was happening in Gaza all the time, talking to people there. Every call with Banias was something I hadn't heard that was completely different from when adults tell the story.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我一直在阅读和思考加沙发生的一切，也一直与那边的人交谈。与 Banias 的每一次通话都让我听到了一些从未听过的、与成年人讲述的版本完全不同的故事。

00:07:40.530 --> 00:08:15.240
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>So that is today's episode. We're calling it "The Narrator." We're going to listen to this kid in Gaza, a narrator who does not ask permission to narrate. She takes the phone with a soaring confidence that what she has to tell you is interesting and important, and I agree with her. Stay with us.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>这就是今天的主题。我们将其命名为《叙述者》。我们将倾听加沙这个孩子的声音，她是一位不需要征得许可便开始叙述的叙述者。她怀着极度的自信拿起电话，认为她所讲述的内容既有趣又重要，我同意她的看法。请继续收听。

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:42.040
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>It's This American Life. My calls with Banias were sporadic. Sometimes we talked once a week. Sometimes a month would go by. Usually, we talked at the end of the day, her time, while she was sitting on a mattress inside the house, fidgeting. There were always lots of people and activity in the background, but Banias never explained much about who was there or what they were doing. She told me about what she was doing, what she wanted me to know and sometimes see.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>这里是《美国生活》。我和 Banias 的通话断断续续。有时我们一周谈一次，有时一个月过去都没有联络。通常我们是在她那边的傍晚通话，那时她正坐在房里的床垫上，坐立不安。背景里总是有很多人和嘈杂的声音，但 Banias 从未多加解释那些人是谁或在做什么。她只会告诉我她在做什么，她想让我知道，有时甚至想让我看什么。

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:44.820
<v Banias>I prefer a video call.
<v Banias>我更喜欢视频通话。

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:46.220
<v Banias>[BEEPING]
<v Banias>[提示音]

00:08:46.220 --> 00:08:47.570
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Let me try.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我试一下。

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:49.070
<v Banias>OK.
<v Banias>好的。

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:51.470
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Hi.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你好。

00:08:51.470 --> 00:08:53.720
<v Banias>This is my complete look.
<v Banias>这就是我的完整造型。

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:55.290
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>That's a good look.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>很棒的造型。

00:08:55.290 --> 00:09:04.710
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>She's in a pink shirt that says "Dream." Huge eyes, dark hair, and pigtails with two loose curls very purposefully framing her face.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她穿着一件印有“Dream”（梦想）字样的粉色衬衫。大眼睛，黑色的头发，两条松散的卷发非常有目的地衬托着她的脸庞。

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:07.410
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And you have earrings. I didn't know you had earrings.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你还戴了耳环。我不知道你有耳环。

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:12.350
<v Banias>Oh, yeah, I do have earrings. And this is my blue shorts.
<v Banias>哦，是的，我有耳环。这是我的蓝色短裤。

00:09:12.350 --> 00:09:13.940
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yeah.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>是啊。

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:20.610
<v Banias>And this, this is my head accessory for today. It has rhinestones.
<v Banias>还有这个，这是我今天的头饰。上面有水钻。

00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:24.380
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Uh-huh. Purple, furry with rhinestones.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>嗯哼。紫色的，毛茸茸的，上面镶着水钻。

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:28.790
<v Banias>Yeah, it's beautiful.
<v Banias>是啊，很漂亮。

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:54.690
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>When Banias and I first started talking on the phone, my questions were pretty basic. What do you do all day? She was in a house with 80 people, which is unusual in Gaza right now to live in a house. Most people are in tents or schools or other temporary shelters. Banias and her mom, dad, and baby brother were on the ground floor of this house, sharing that floor with about 20 relatives. There was one bedroom.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>当我和 Banias 开始通电话时，我的问题都很基础。你整天都在做什么？她当时住在一间有 80 个人的房子里，这在目前的加沙是不常见的。大多数人都住在帐篷、学校或其他临时避难所里。Banias 和她的父母及弟弟住在房子的底层，与大约 20 位亲戚共用这层空间。只有一个卧室。

00:09:54.690 --> 00:10:12.180
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>She slept on a mattress on the floor, alongside her parents, brother, grandpa, uncle, and aunt. Everyone else slept in the living area. If Banias wanted any time in the tiny bathroom, she got up early in the morning. Then she ate breakfast. And then what?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她和父母、弟弟、祖父、叔叔和阿姨一起睡在地板上的床垫上。其他人都睡在起居区。如果 Banias 想在那个狭小的浴室里待一会儿，她得一大早起床。然后吃早餐。接着做什么呢？

00:10:12.180 --> 00:10:16.350
<v Banias>Today we play school games.
<v Banias>今天我们玩学校游戏。

00:10:16.350 --> 00:10:18.150
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What does that mean?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>那是什么意思？

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:29.970
<v Banias>We're pretending that we're in the school. I was a student. And one of my friends was the teacher.
<v Banias>我们假装在学校。我是一个学生。我的一个朋友是老师。

00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:33.090
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What classes were you taking?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你们在上什么课？

00:10:33.090 --> 00:10:34.630
<v Banias>Math class.
<v Banias>数学课。

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:40.500
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>OK. And did you write actual math, or is it just pretend?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>好的。你们是真的在写数学题，还是假装的？

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:53.560
<v Banias>It was actual, the plus and the minus and the equal. It was actual. But it was in a game, not real.
<v Banias>是真的，有加法、减法和等号。是真的在做题。但这只是个游戏，不是真的上学。

00:10:53.560 --> 00:11:12.970
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>At this point, July, Banias had not been in an actual class in an actual school building for nine months. But she played school every day with three other girls, two younger and one older. There were other kids in the building, but everyone else was just OK, or a boy, or a baby.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>此时是七月，Banias 已经九个月没有在真正的教学楼里上过真正的课了。但她每天都和另外三个女孩一起玩“学校游戏”，两个比她小，一个比她大。楼里还有其他孩子，但其他人要么只是还行，要么是男孩，要么是婴儿。

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:39.450
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>When aid organizations go into other war zones, one of the first things they do for kids is set up schools, because children need a sense of routine and a sense that life is moving forward toward a future. There's no safe place in Gaza to set up schools like that, so Banias and her friends in the building created that for themselves. They played school for hours. There were lectures. There were assignments. There were exams.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>当援助组织进入其他战区时，他们为孩子做的第一件事就是建立学校，因为孩子们需要一种日常感，需要一种生活正在向前、通往未来的感觉。在加沙没有安全的地方建立这样的学校，所以 Banias 和她在楼里的朋友们为自己创造了这样的环境。她们玩了好几个小时的学校游戏。有讲座，有作业，还有考试。

00:11:39.450 --> 00:11:44.820
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Who is usually in charge of what you're going to do that day?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>通常谁负责决定你们当天要做什么？

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:48.970
<v Banias>The girl that's older than me. Her name is Dana.
<v Banias>那个比我大的女孩。她叫 Dana。

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:52.500
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>How old is Dana?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Dana 多大了？

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:57.420
<v Banias>She is 12 years old. And she has an iPad.
<v Banias>她 12 岁了。她有一台 iPad。

00:11:57.420 --> 00:12:16.860
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Dana is generous with her iPad. So this is another part of Banias's day-- games on the iPad. When the war started, her mother's screen time rules went out the window. But also, Israel cut off electricity to Gaza. There's just generators and solar panels, so screen time is limited anyway.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Dana 对她的 iPad 很慷慨。所以这是 Banias 日常生活的另一部分——玩 iPad 游戏。战争开始时，她妈妈对屏幕时间的限制就不复存在了。但同时，以色列切断了加沙的电力。只有发电机和太阳能电池板，所以屏幕使用时间无论如何都很有限。

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:21.880
<v Banias>And today, we played a cafe game.
<v Banias>今天，我们玩了咖啡馆游戏。

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:24.720
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Oh, a cafe? That's new.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>哦，咖啡馆？那是新花样。

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:36.660
<v Banias>I was the chef. Yeah. And one of my friends was the customer. I cooked some salad and some pancake.
<v Banias>我是厨师。是的。我的一个朋友是顾客。我做了一些沙拉和煎饼。

00:12:36.660 --> 00:12:39.280
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Say it one more time?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>再说一遍？

00:12:39.280 --> 00:12:46.630
<v Banias>I cooked salad and pancake. And I made some hamburgers and some pizza.
<v Banias>我做了沙拉和煎饼。我还做了汉堡和披萨。

00:12:46.630 --> 00:12:56.230
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Banias was re-enacting her old life, where she had teachers and exams and went out to cafes. There was one they used to go to every Saturday.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Banias 正在重温她的旧生活，那时候她有老师，有考试，还会去咖啡馆。他们以前每周六都会去一家咖啡馆。

00:12:56.230 --> 00:13:02.930
<v Banias>Yeah, it was really close. It was just in the next street in our house.
<v Banias>是的，离我们很近。就在我们房子旁边的下一条街上。

00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:08.470
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>OK. Did they make salad and pancakes?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>好的。他们卖沙拉和煎饼吗？

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:16.190
<v Banias>No, but I used to order some noodles and some hot chocolate.
<v Banias>不，但我以前常点面条和热巧克力。

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:22.900
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Mm-hmm. What did you eat in real life today?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>嗯哼。你今天现实中吃了什么？

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:32.200
<v Banias>Today we have eaten some beans, some white beans.
<v Banias>今天我们吃了一些豆子，白豆。

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:38.420
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Do you ever get to eat pancakes or noodles or burgers?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你有时能吃到煎饼、面条或汉堡吗？

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:42.030
<v Banias>I hate pancakes and noodles.
<v Banias>我讨厌煎饼和面条。

00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:43.820
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>You do?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>真的吗？

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:44.780
<v Banias>Yes.
<v Banias>是的。

00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:47.030
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Oh, wow.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>哦，天哪。

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:50.730
<v Banias>Do you believe somebody hates these things?
<v Banias>你相信有人会讨厌这些东西吗？

00:13:50.730 --> 00:13:51.090
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>No.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>不信。

00:13:51.090 --> 00:13:51.630
<v Banias>I do.
<v Banias>我就讨厌。

00:13:51.630 --> 00:13:54.380
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>They're so good.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>它们明明那么好吃。

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:59.810
<v Banias>But I hate them.
<v Banias>但我就是讨厌它们。

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:12.770
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>I was never sure what motivated Banias to want to talk to me. She seemed to like telling me about her day, practicing her English. She had an ongoing fascination with the time difference between us. She always wanted to check in on that.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我一直不确定是什么动力让 Banias 想和我说话。她似乎很喜欢告诉我她的一天，练习她的英语。她对我们之间的时间差一直很着迷。她总是想确认这一点。

00:14:12.770 --> 00:14:15.540
<v Banias>You're at morning or at night?
<v Banias>你是早上还是晚上？

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:18.470
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>It's the afternoon. It's just--
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>现在是下午。只是——

00:14:18.470 --> 00:14:19.380
<v Banias>Afternoon?
<v Banias>下午？

00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:20.390
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Mm-hmm.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>嗯哼。

00:14:20.390 --> 00:14:22.880
<v Banias>We're in the middle of the night.
<v Banias>我们这里是半夜。

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:28.260
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>She'd call when she felt annoyed that Dana got to be the teacher that day yet again.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>当她因为 Dana 那天又当了老师而感到烦恼时，她会打电话给我。

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:38.310
<v Banias>I am bored of being the student every day. I'm the oldest. I should be the teacher. Oof!
<v Banias>我厌倦了每天都当学生。我是最大的，我应该当老师。哎！

00:14:38.310 --> 00:15:01.270
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And she'd call when she was bored. She'd call because I was an adult who would pay attention to her. Banias had to create activity-- interest-- out of such little material. Sometimes I got the impression I was there to help with that. Like, one night she was on the phone with me, and another phone rang. And like a character in a play, she went, oh, look, the phone is ringing.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她也会在感到无聊时打电话给我。她会打来是因为我是一个会关注她的成年人。Banias 必须从极其有限的素材中创造出活动和趣味。有时我觉得我的存在就是为了帮助她实现这一点。比如，有一天她正在和我通话时，另一部电话响了。她就像戏里的角色一样说，哦，看，电话响了。

00:15:01.270 --> 00:15:02.040
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>[PHONE RINGING]
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>[电话响声]

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:07.820
<v Banias>Oh, my God. Who's ringing the phone? Get away. Get lost.
<v Banias>天哪。是谁在打电话？走开。滚远点。

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:09.630
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>[LAUGHS]
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>[笑]

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:12.570
<v Banias>We have to sleep.
<v Banias>我们要睡觉了。

00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:14.850
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>You're pretty funny, Banias.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你真幽默，Banias。

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:21.670
<v Banias>Yes, I'm funny. Dana always say for me that I'm a bit funny.
<v Banias>是的，我很幽默。Dana 总说我很有趣。

00:15:21.670 --> 00:15:22.020
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Really?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>真的吗？

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:22.860
<v Banias>Funny bunny.
<v Banias>趣萌兔。

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:24.280
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Mm-hmm. You are funny.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>嗯哼。你确实很有趣。

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:27.030
<v Banias>Yes. I'm a funny bunny.
<v Banias>是的。我是一只趣萌兔。

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:46.250
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>So Banias had her own reasons to call me. When I called her, it was for different reasons. I'd call her because I'd read about a bombing campaign or fighting near where she was. Was she OK? And what was she thinking about all the violence around her? What is this like for an eight-year-old?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>所以 Banias 有她自己的理由打电话给我。而我打给她，是出于不同的原因。我会打给她是因为我读到了关于她所在地区附近的轰炸或冲突的新闻。她还好吗？对于周围所有的暴力，她是怎么想的？这对一个八岁的孩子来说意味着什么？

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:58.700
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>In the middle of the summer, there was a series of intense airstrikes near Banias. I was curious if she'd heard them or seen them, but I also wanted to follow her lead and what she wanted to talk about.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>在夏天的中期，Banias 附近发生了一系列剧烈的空袭。我很好奇她是否听到了或看到了，但我同时也想顺着她的思路，关注她想谈论的话题。

00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:01.820
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Do you have some time to talk?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你有时间聊聊吗？

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:04.560
<v Banias>Oh, yes, of course. I'm available.
<v Banias>哦，当然，我有空。

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:05.450
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Great.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>太好了。

00:16:05.450 --> 00:16:07.770
<v Banias>I'm actually good.
<v Banias>我其实挺好的。

00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:08.540
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yeah?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>是吗？

00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:19.810
<v Banias>Doing good. Last days, we have heard a bit of bombing around us.
<v Banias>做得不错。最近几天，我们听到附近有一些爆炸声。

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:26.120
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Uh-huh. Yeah, I've been reading in the news that there's been a lot of bombing.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>嗯哼。是的，我在新闻里读到那里有很多轰炸。

00:16:26.120 --> 00:16:32.160
<v Banias>Yeah, I do know. It was loud.
<v Banias>我知道。声音很大。

00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:35.760
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Is it scary?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>这可怕吗？

00:16:35.760 --> 00:17:02.700
<v Banias>No. For me, no. Me and my friends, we were playing hide-and-seek. We don't ever get bored of it. It's our favorite game. When we are playing, some strange things happens with us. I will tell you then.
<v Banias>不可怕。对我来说不可怕。我和朋友们在玩捉迷藏。我们永远不会对这游戏感到厌烦。这是我们最喜欢的游戏。当我们玩的时候，会发生一些奇怪的事情。我到时候会告诉你的。

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:15.970
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>OK, I thought. Here it is. She's about to tell me something big about what it's like to be a kid playing hide-and-seek with bombs going off nearby. Banias told me, so we were playing, and we ran to the backyard.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>好的，我想。来了。她要告诉我关于在炮火声中玩捉迷藏的重大感受了。Banias 告诉我，我们当时正在玩，然后跑到了后院。

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:25.870
<v Banias>When we run to the backyard, we see some insects in the ground.
<v Banias>当我们跑进后院时，我们看到地上有一些昆虫。

00:17:25.870 --> 00:17:27.270
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Mm-hmm.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>嗯哼。

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:35.620
<v Banias>We said, we see some insects on the ground. And me and the kids, we watched it.
<v Banias>我们说，我们看到地上有一些昆虫。然后我和孩子们就盯着看。

00:17:35.620 --> 00:17:54.460
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>That's it. That's her whole story. The strange thing that happened when they ran outside is they saw insects, a kind of insect they'd never seen before. Not the bombing-- bugs.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>就这样。这就是她的全部故事。她们跑出去时发生的奇怪的事情就是她们看到了一些昆虫，一种她们从未见过的昆虫。不是轰炸，而是虫子。

00:17:54.460 --> 00:18:10.790
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Children are not known for their sense of scale or the longevity of their attention. And maybe it wasn't surprising that pretty much every time I asked about the war, Banias didn't really want to engage. She didn't exactly ignore me, but it didn't seem to be the main thing she was thinking about.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>孩子们并不以衡量尺度或长时间专注而闻名。所以，每当我问起战争时，Banias 并不太想深入讨论，这也就不足为奇了。她没有完全忽略我，但这似乎并不是她心中主要的想法。

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:31.660
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Like, when an airstrike broke the windows in her house, she wanted to tell me about a prank she played on Dana. In mid-August, when ceasefire negotiations between Israel and Hamas seemed to be unraveling yet again, and all the adults I was talking to in Gaza were deeply dispirited, here was Banias.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>比如，当空袭震碎了她家里的窗户时，她却想告诉我她对 Dana 搞的一个恶作剧。八月中旬，当以色列和哈马斯之间的停火谈判似乎再次破裂时，我在加沙交谈的所有成年人都感到极度沮丧，但 Banias 却是这样。

00:18:31.660 --> 00:18:34.810
<v Banias>I think there will be a ceasefire soon.
<v Banias>我想很快就会停火的。

00:18:34.810 --> 00:18:39.160
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>You do? Why do you think that?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你觉得呢？为什么这么想？

00:18:39.160 --> 00:18:46.420
<v Banias>Because it's really close to end.
<v Banias>因为它快要结束了。

00:18:46.420 --> 00:18:51.220
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Why? Why do you say-- what gives you that idea?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>为什么？为什么你会这么说——是什么让你有这种想法？

00:18:51.220 --> 00:18:55.540
<v Banias>Mom and Dad tell me. [YAWNS]
<v Banias>爸爸妈妈告诉我的。[打哈欠]

00:18:55.540 --> 00:19:21.020
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>I heard that yawn-- noting it. Discussion of the war-- over. There was one moment when Banias was forced to engage. She couldn't avoid it. Banias's family had been sheltering in Deir Balah for almost a year, when, suddenly, at the end of August, they got an evacuation order. Israel posted a map on social media designating certain blocks in Deir Balah unsafe.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我听到那个哈欠了——记下来。关于战争的讨论——到此为止。有一次，Banias 不得不面对现实。她无法回避。Banias 的一家在代尔拜拉赫避难了近一年，这时突然在八月底，他们接到了撤离命令。以色列在社交媒体上发布了一张地图，将代尔拜拉赫的某些区域指定为不安全区域。

00:19:21.020 --> 00:19:45.130
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And I saw that Maram, Banias's mother, had written something for Al Jazeera about the order. I had hardly spoken to Maram for months, but I had followed her reporting on bombings and food shortages. This article, though, was personal. She wrote about her confusion about what to do next. "I've never felt so worthless as a human being," she wrote.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我看到 Banias 的母亲 Maram 为半岛电视台写了一些关于这个命令的文章。我有好几个月没和 Maram 说上话了，但我一直关注着她关于轰炸和粮食短缺的报道。然而这篇文章非常私人。她写下了她对下一步该做什么的困惑。“作为一个人类，我从未感到如此无用，”她写道。

00:19:45.130 --> 00:20:13.400
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>"A single Facebook post from an Israeli military spokesperson can upend our lives in an instant. Have you ever felt like a toy being played with left and right, east and west, pushed from one place to another, south to Khan Younis, out of Rafah, back to Khan Younis, then to Nuseirat, only to be driven out again? People are literally running through the streets like mad, clutching what little they have left. We have nothing left. Our hearts are broken, and our minds are frayed.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>“以色列军方发言人的一条 Facebook 帖子就能瞬间颠覆我们的生活。你有没有感觉自己像一个被玩弄于股掌之间的玩具，被从东到西、从左到右，从一个地方推向另一个地方——向南逃往汗尤尼斯，离开拉法，回到汗尤尼斯，然后去努赛拉特，最后又被驱逐？人们真的像疯了一样在街上奔跑，紧紧抓着他们仅存的一点东西。我们一无所有了。我们的心碎了，精神也崩溃了。”

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:47.550
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>I look around at the few possessions I've managed to gather over the past 10 months-- a stove, cups, plates, pots, winter clothes, summer clothes, mattresses, blankets, batteries, light bulbs, big bottles of drinking water, tubs to wash clothes in. If I leave everything, there's no way to replace it. There are no markets, no supplies, no money to spare. We're running and running aimlessly. People screaming, suffering, and dying while the world watches," end quote. And then my phone rang.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>“我环顾四周，看看过去 10 个月里我设法收集到的几样东西——一个炉子、杯子、盘子、锅、冬装、夏装、床垫、毯子、电池、灯泡、大瓶饮用水、洗衣服的盆。如果我丢下这一切，我就没法再添置了。没有市场，没有补给，没有多余的钱。我们就在那里漫无目的地奔跑。人们在尖叫、受苦、死亡，而世界在注视，”引用结束。接着，我的电话响了。

00:20:47.550 --> 00:20:53.390
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Hello?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>喂？

00:20:53.390 --> 00:20:54.830
<v Banias>Hello?
<v Banias>喂？

00:20:54.830 --> 00:20:57.050
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Hi, Banias.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你好，Banias。

00:20:57.050 --> 00:20:59.630
<v Banias>Yeah.
<v Banias>在呢。

00:20:59.630 --> 00:21:02.120
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Do you want to talk?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>想聊聊吗？

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:09.680
<v Banias>Uh, OK. Today, we have done a new thing.
<v Banias>呃，好的。今天我们做了一件新鲜事。

00:21:09.680 --> 00:21:11.900
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What'd you do?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>做了什么？

00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:23.800
<v Banias>We drawed some pictures. I imagined that there's a garden, that there's some people walking inside it.
<v Banias>我们画了一些画。我想象有一个花园，有一些人在里面散步。

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:25.470
<v Banias>[CHILD CRYING]
<v Banias>[孩子哭泣声]

00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:29.280
<v Banias>Stop crying. Go in the bedroom.
<v Banias>别哭了。去卧室里。

00:21:29.280 --> 00:21:31.080
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>OK.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>好的。

00:21:31.080 --> 00:21:32.310
<v Banias>So let's continue.
<v Banias>那我们继续。

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:33.360
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>OK.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>好的。

00:21:33.360 --> 00:21:45.570
<v Banias>Oh, my friends were with me, too, drawing. And one of my friends have drawed a plane.
<v Banias>哦，我的朋友们也在和我一起画。我的一个朋友画了一架飞机。

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:50.580
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Like a war plane or a plane you travel in?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>是像战机还是那种旅行的飞机？

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:52.000
<v Banias>Uh, traveling.
<v Banias>呃，旅行的。

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:59.550
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>OK. Do you ever draw anything about the war?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>好的。你画过任何关于战争的东西吗？

00:21:59.550 --> 00:22:01.440
<v Banias>No, nothing at all.
<v Banias>没有，一点也没有。

00:22:01.440 --> 00:22:03.780
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Why not?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>为什么不呢？

00:22:03.780 --> 00:22:11.520
<v Banias>Because-- I really can't.
<v Banias>因为——我真的不能。

00:22:11.520 --> 00:22:13.350
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Why?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>为什么？

00:22:13.350 --> 00:22:16.020
<v Banias>I feel mad.
<v Banias>我感到生气。

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:17.010
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Uh-huh.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>嗯哼。

00:22:17.010 --> 00:23:05.390
<v Banias>I feel mad of this things. I can draw them. But I don't like a war plane, a helicopter, and rockets. I don't like that. There's lots of things here I feel mad from it. My friends always make me mad from things. Sometimes I don't want anybody to enter this room. Get out. Mom! OK.
<v Banias>我对这些事情感到生气。我可以画它们，但我一点也不喜欢战机、直升机和火箭。我不喜欢这些。这里有很多让我生气的事情。我的朋友们总是因为一些事情让我生气。有时我不想让任何人进入这个房间。出去。妈妈！好的。

00:23:05.390 --> 00:23:06.710
<v Maram Hamaid>I'm sorry.
<v Maram Hamaid>抱歉。

00:23:06.710 --> 00:23:08.610
<v Banias>OK, let's continue.
<v Banias>好的，我们继续。

00:23:08.610 --> 00:23:09.350
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>OK.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>好的。

00:23:09.350 --> 00:23:13.620
<v Banias>I was saying they always attack me.
<v Banias>我刚才说她们总是攻击我。

00:23:13.620 --> 00:23:15.470
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Your friends?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你的朋友们？

00:23:15.470 --> 00:23:16.910
<v Banias>Yeah.
<v Banias>是的。

00:23:16.910 --> 00:23:34.960
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>I was eager to ask Banias about the news of the evacuation, but what she wanted to talk about was a fight she had that day with another kid in the building, a girl. Banias calls her "the girl with the bad personality." That girl told Banias today that one of her pictures was no good.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我很想问 Banias 关于撤离命令的新闻，但她想聊的却是那天她和楼里另一个孩子——一个女孩——之间的争执。Banias 称她为“那个性格坏的女孩”。那个女孩今天告诉 Banias，她的画画得不好。

00:23:34.960 --> 00:23:45.460
<v Banias>She have a really bad personality. I said for her, are you looking for a fight, in our language.
<v Banias>她的性格真的很差。我用我们的语言对她说，你是想打架吗？

00:23:45.460 --> 00:23:48.630
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And what did she say?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她说什么？

00:23:48.630 --> 00:23:49.850
<v Banias>Yes, I am.
<v Banias>是的，我是。

00:23:49.850 --> 00:23:51.390
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>[LAUGHS]
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>[笑]

00:23:51.390 --> 00:23:57.600
<v Banias>And we fighted all day. She's the most bad friend.
<v Banias>我们就这样打了一整天。她是最坏的朋友。

00:23:57.600 --> 00:24:05.550
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Did she not know about the evacuation order? She must, right? I didn't want to scare her.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>难道她不知道撤离命令吗？她肯定知道，对吧？我不想吓到她。

00:24:05.550 --> 00:24:12.850
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Banias, I saw your mom wrote about people leaving Deir Balah.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Banias，我看到你妈妈写关于人们离开代尔拜拉赫的事情了。

00:24:12.850 --> 00:24:13.410
<v Banias>Yes.
<v Banias>是的。

00:24:13.410 --> 00:24:14.020
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Have you--
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你有没有——

00:24:14.020 --> 00:24:18.650
<v Banias>But we will go to Al-Zawayda, to our relatives.
<v Banias>但我们会去 Al-Zawayda，去我们的亲戚那里。

00:24:18.650 --> 00:24:20.990
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What do you think about that?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你怎么想？

00:24:20.990 --> 00:24:40.730
<v Banias>I think it was a good idea. We're packing our clothes and our-- wait for a minute. [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH] Oh, and we're packing also our mattresses and our money.
<v Banias>我觉得这是个好主意。我们正在打包衣服和我们的……等一下。[非英语对话] 哦，我们还在打包床垫和钱。

00:24:40.730 --> 00:24:46.560
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Where will you sleep if you pack your mattress?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>如果你打包了床垫，你们睡哪里？

00:24:46.560 --> 00:24:59.890
<v Banias>Um, in the tent. Our relatives live in a home. But we will make a camp next to them.
<v Banias>嗯，在帐篷里。我们的亲戚住在房子里，但我们会在他们旁边搭个营地。

00:24:59.890 --> 00:25:05.260
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>OK. Have you ever lived in a tent?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>好的。你以前住过帐篷吗？

00:25:05.260 --> 00:25:07.240
<v Banias>No.
<v Banias>没有。

00:25:07.240 --> 00:25:08.180
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Are you--
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你是——

00:25:08.180 --> 00:25:14.370
<v Banias>But I want to try. I think it will be something creative.
<v Banias>但我很想试试。我想那会很有创意。

00:25:14.370 --> 00:25:21.270
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Are you scared to move, to leave your friends or to leave your house?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你害怕搬家，离开你的朋友或房子吗？

00:25:21.270 --> 00:25:23.530
<v Banias>I'm ready to leave them.
<v Banias>我已经准备好离开她们了。

00:25:23.530 --> 00:25:25.290
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>You are? [CHUCKLES]
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>是吗？[轻笑]

00:25:25.290 --> 00:25:42.130
<v Banias>I'm not ready for more fights. I want to leave them. Today, I told one of my friends that I will leave. I've told everybody.
<v Banias>我不想再打架了。我想离开她们。今天，我告诉其中一个朋友我要走了。我告诉了所有人。

00:25:42.130 --> 00:25:43.770
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Is that sad?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>那令人难过吗？

00:25:43.770 --> 00:25:45.520
<v Banias>It was drama.
<v Banias>那简直是一场闹剧。

00:25:45.520 --> 00:25:48.390
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Why?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>为什么？

00:25:48.390 --> 00:25:55.870
<v Banias>Because she is a drama girl. Don't leave. That's everything.
<v Banias>因为她是个爱闹剧的女孩。别走。就是这样。

00:25:55.870 --> 00:25:57.090
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Uh-huh.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>嗯哼。

00:25:57.090 --> 00:26:03.120
<v Banias>Don't leave this house. We want more fights.
<v Banias>别离开这房子。我们还要再打架呢。

00:26:03.120 --> 00:26:19.180
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Banias was ready to leave because it meant she could get away from the girl with the bad personality. Almost a million kids in Gaza have made a move like this since Israel invaded, many of them multiple times. So it was interesting to hear how a child was thinking about it.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Banias 准备离开，因为这意味着她可以远离那个性格糟糕的女孩。自从以色列入侵以来，加沙有近一百万孩子像这样搬过家，很多人还是多次搬迁。所以听听一个孩子对此的思考很有趣。

00:26:19.180 --> 00:26:36.820
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Banias was ready to flee the home she'd lived in for 10 months at that point, to move into a tent because she got into a fight with an annoying girl that day, because that is what just happened-- and because Banias is eight. She told me her friend Dana is leaving, too.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Banias 准备逃离她住了 10 个月的家，搬进帐篷，仅仅是因为她那天和一个讨厌的女孩打了一架——因为这就是刚刚发生的事——也因为 Banias 才八岁。她告诉我她的朋友 Dana 也要走了。

00:26:36.820 --> 00:26:57.100
<v Banias>She is going to Al Mawasi. But me, I will go to Zawayda, me and my family. Yeah, our relatives are there. When the Israeli army tell us to move, we'll move to Al Zawayda.
<v Banias>她要去 Al Mawasi。但我，我会去 Zawayda，我和我的家人。是的，我们的亲戚在那边。当以色列军队叫我们离开时，我们会搬到 Al Zawayda。

00:26:57.100 --> 00:26:59.820
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>You're not scared?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你不害怕吗？

00:26:59.820 --> 00:27:04.030
<v Banias>[YAWNS] No.
<v Banias>[打哈欠] 不怕。

00:27:04.030 --> 00:27:04.670
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>OK.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>好的。

00:27:04.670 --> 00:27:09.010
<v Maram Hamaid>[INAUDIBLE] crying and he was praying.
<v Maram Hamaid>[听不清] 哭着，他当时正在祈祷。

00:27:09.010 --> 00:27:11.910
<v Banias>Mom, let that a secret!
<v Banias>妈妈，让那成为秘密！

00:27:11.910 --> 00:27:15.890
<v Maram Hamaid>No, it's not a secret. You have to express yourself.
<v Maram Hamaid>不，这不是秘密。你必须表达你的感受。

00:27:15.890 --> 00:27:18.590
<v Banias>I'm fine, I'm fine.
<v Banias>我没事，我没事。

00:27:18.590 --> 00:27:23.230
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What does your mom think is a secret?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你妈妈认为什么是秘密？

00:27:23.230 --> 00:27:40.530
<v Banias>Uh-- a family secret. No. No. I will not give you the mobile. I want to talk to her myself. No, [INAUDIBLE]. No, no.
<v Banias>呃——一个家庭秘密。不。不。我不给你手机了。我想亲自和她谈。不，[听不清]。不，不。

00:27:40.530 --> 00:27:41.630
<v Maram Hamaid>Is that Chana?
<v Maram Hamaid>是 Chana 吗？

00:27:41.630 --> 00:27:42.830
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Hi.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你好。

00:27:42.830 --> 00:27:43.800
<v Maram Hamaid>Hi. How are you?
<v Maram Hamaid>你好。你好吗？

00:27:43.800 --> 00:27:44.390
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Good.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>很好。

00:27:44.390 --> 00:27:50.040
<v Banias>No, no! Let that away! Let that away! Let that away!
<v Banias>不，不！把那个拿走！拿走！拿走！

00:27:50.040 --> 00:27:50.600
<v Maram Hamaid>I was just--
<v Maram Hamaid>我只是——

00:27:50.600 --> 00:27:52.300
<v Banias>No, no! Let that away.
<v Banias>不，不！拿走。

00:27:52.300 --> 00:27:53.450
<v Maram Hamaid>--I just heard her--
<v Maram Hamaid>——我刚才听到她——

00:27:53.450 --> 00:27:54.330
<v Banias>Please, please!
<v Banias>拜托，拜托！

00:27:54.330 --> 00:27:54.900
<v Maram Hamaid>--saying that--
<v Maram Hamaid>——说那个——

00:27:54.900 --> 00:27:55.230
<v Banias>Not here!
<v Banias>不要在这！

00:27:55.230 --> 00:27:55.760
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Your--
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你的——

00:27:55.760 --> 00:27:57.030
<v Maram Hamaid>So Banias was crying.
<v Maram Hamaid>所以 Banias 在哭。

00:27:57.030 --> 00:27:59.750
<v Banias>No! Can you keep that away?
<v Banias>不！你能把那个拿走吗？

00:27:59.750 --> 00:28:00.780
<v Maram Hamaid>It's normal.
<v Maram Hamaid>这很正常。

00:28:00.780 --> 00:28:03.230
<v Banias>It's a secret. I don't want--
<v Banias>这是个秘密。我不想——

00:28:03.230 --> 00:28:03.960
<v Maram Hamaid>This is normal.
<v Maram Hamaid>这很正常。

00:28:03.960 --> 00:28:08.720
<v Banias>I don't want to let anybody know that I was-- I wasn't!
<v Banias>我不想让任何人知道我当时——我没哭！

00:28:08.720 --> 00:28:09.310
<v Maram Hamaid>No.
<v Maram Hamaid>不。

00:28:09.310 --> 00:28:10.480
<v Banias>No, I was--
<v Banias>不，我是——

00:28:10.480 --> 00:28:10.890
<v Maram Hamaid>You were crying.
<v Maram Hamaid>你在哭。

00:28:10.890 --> 00:28:12.400
<v Banias>--I wasn't!
<v Banias>——我没哭！

00:28:12.400 --> 00:28:18.730
<v Maram Hamaid>So she was afraid. She was nervous. And she went into--
<v Maram Hamaid>所以她很害怕。她很紧张。她进入了一个——

00:28:18.730 --> 00:28:19.630
<v Banias>I was not afraid!
<v Banias>我没害怕！

00:28:19.630 --> 00:28:20.280
<v Maram Hamaid>--a circle--
<v Maram Hamaid>——循环——

00:28:20.280 --> 00:28:21.610
<v Banias>I was not nervous!
<v Banias>我不紧张！

00:28:21.610 --> 00:28:24.450
<v Maram Hamaid>--of feeling sad and feeling nervous--
<v Maram Hamaid>——感到难过和紧张的循环——

00:28:24.450 --> 00:28:25.540
<v Banias>[INAUDIBLE] Keep that away!
<v Banias>[听不清] 把那个拿走！

00:28:25.540 --> 00:28:31.710
<v Maram Hamaid>--very afraid of what is going on. And I just surprisingly heard her saying that I'm not.
<v Maram Hamaid>——非常害怕正在发生的事情。而我居然惊讶地听到她说她没有。

00:28:31.710 --> 00:28:32.260
<v Banias>Let that away!
<v Banias>把那个拿走！

00:28:32.260 --> 00:28:35.150
<v Maram Hamaid>I didn't feel afraid.
<v Maram Hamaid>我没感到害怕。

00:28:35.150 --> 00:28:36.820
<v Banias>Let that away!
<v Banias>把那个拿走！

00:28:36.820 --> 00:28:39.770
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Why? Why does she not want to talk about that?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>为什么？为什么她不想谈论那个？

00:28:39.770 --> 00:28:53.380
<v Maram Hamaid>And she's now saying that it's a secret. Like, she doesn't want to recall some horrific memories for her, or like she got over the feeling of being afraid.
<v Maram Hamaid>现在她说这是个秘密。就好像她不想回忆起那些恐怖的记忆，或者好像她已经克服了那种恐惧感。

00:28:53.380 --> 00:28:56.650
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>When did she find out you were evacuating?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她是什么时候知道你们要撤离的？

00:28:56.650 --> 00:28:57.590
<v Maram Hamaid>Excuse me?
<v Maram Hamaid>对不起？

00:28:57.590 --> 00:28:59.210
<v Banias>I didn't cry!
<v Banias>我没哭！

00:28:59.210 --> 00:29:00.130
<v Maram Hamaid>[CHUCKLES]
<v Maram Hamaid>[轻笑]

00:29:00.130 --> 00:29:02.410
<v Banias>I didn't cry!
<v Banias>我没哭！

00:29:02.410 --> 00:29:23.270
<v Maram Hamaid>Hallas, she believes you. She believes you. She believes you. I know. Like, you're a brave girl. Like, you can get over anything. But I'm telling you, Banias. It's not a shame. It's not a shameful thing to feel afraid that you're scared and you're afraid of something like this. Yeah? So--
<v Maram Hamaid>好啦，她相信你。她相信你。她相信你。我知道。你是勇敢的女孩。你能克服任何困难。但我告诉你，Banias，这并不羞耻。对于感到害怕、对于这种事感到恐惧并不是什么可耻的事。是吧？所以——

00:29:23.270 --> 00:29:23.720
<v Banias>So--
<v Banias>所以——

00:29:23.720 --> 00:29:29.680
<v Maram Hamaid>--right? It's normal. You should be scared. Yeah, this is very normal.
<v Maram Hamaid>——对吧？这很正常。你应该感到害怕。是的，这非常正常。

00:29:29.680 --> 00:29:30.270
<v Banias>I was not--
<v Banias>我没——

00:29:30.270 --> 00:29:31.660
<v Maram Hamaid>And do what I can.
<v Maram Hamaid>尽我所能。

00:29:31.660 --> 00:29:32.840
<v Banias>--scared!
<v Banias>——害怕！

00:29:32.840 --> 00:29:54.030
<v Maram Hamaid>OK, Mama, you are hallas. You are afraid to say what you want. But I want to just to clarify this point. [LAUGHS] You were crying like crazy upon hearing the news. And I'm telling her, like I totally understand her feelings.
<v Maram Hamaid>好的，妈妈，好啦。你不敢说你想说的话。但我只想澄清这一点。[笑] 你听到消息时哭得稀里哗啦。我告诉她，我完全理解她的感受。

00:29:54.030 --> 00:29:57.860
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>When did that happen, Maram? When did you tell her?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>那是什么时候发生的，Maram？你是什么时候告诉她的？

00:29:57.860 --> 00:30:01.050
<v Maram Hamaid>It's just less than two hours ago.
<v Maram Hamaid>就在不到两小时前。

00:30:01.050 --> 00:30:03.750
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Oh, wow, just recently. OK. OK.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>哦，天哪，就在刚才。好的。好的。

00:30:03.750 --> 00:30:23.560
<v Maram Hamaid>Yeah, yeah, yeah. Very recent, you know? Very recent. We got the news suddenly. [LAUGHS] I was really laughing when I heard her trying to show a perfectionist reaction and so positive. She was very positive.
<v Maram Hamaid>是啊，是啊，是啊。非常近，你知道吗？非常近。我们突然收到了消息。[笑] 我听到她试图表现出完美主义者的反应，表现得非常积极时，真的笑了。她非常乐观。

00:30:23.560 --> 00:30:43.980
<v Maram Hamaid>But it was totally the opposite, you know? Just, like, two hours, less than two hours, she was hiding behind the curtain, crying and like crazy. And she continued this cycle. And then we find it's really hard.
<v Maram Hamaid>但事实完全相反，你知道吗？就在不到两小时前，她躲在窗帘后面，哭得像疯了一样。她不断陷入这种循环。然后我们发现这真的很难。

00:30:43.980 --> 00:31:01.770
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>I almost couldn't bear hearing this. Banias's visceral, immediate panic was so uncomfortable, hearing her mother pierce the carefully constructed artifice she'd presented to me. And it was disorienting. It made me think of all the things I didn't know.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我几乎无法忍受听到这些。Banias 发自肺腑、直接的恐慌让人如此不安，听到她母亲撕开了她在我面前精心构建的虚假外壳。这让人感到迷失方向。这让我想到所有我所不知道的事情。

00:31:01.770 --> 00:31:03.940
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Does she want to talk again?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她想再谈谈吗？

00:31:03.940 --> 00:31:05.840
<v Maram Hamaid>Yeah, yeah. She's here. She's here.
<v Maram Hamaid>想的，她在这里。她在这里。

00:31:05.840 --> 00:31:07.030
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>OK.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>好的。

00:31:07.030 --> 00:31:08.290
<v Maram Hamaid>[INAUDIBLE] come and [INAUDIBLE]
<v Maram Hamaid>[听不清] 过来和 [听不清]

00:31:08.290 --> 00:31:09.100
<v Banias>Hello?
<v Banias>喂？

00:31:09.100 --> 00:31:11.440
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Hi, Banias.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你好，Banias。

00:31:11.440 --> 00:31:11.930
<v Banias>Hi.
<v Banias>你好。

00:31:11.930 --> 00:31:18.820
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Hi. How come you didn't want me to know that you were upset?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你好。为什么你不想让我知道你很难过？

00:31:18.820 --> 00:31:20.210
<v Banias>I'm not upset.
<v Banias>我不难过。

00:31:20.210 --> 00:31:26.370
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>You're not upset. Do you want to talk about that or no?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你不难过。你想谈谈那个吗，还是不想？

00:31:26.370 --> 00:31:27.780
<v Banias>Not yet.
<v Banias>还没到时候。

00:31:27.780 --> 00:31:30.340
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>什么？

00:31:30.340 --> 00:31:32.200
<v Banias>Not yet.
<v Banias>还没到时候。

00:31:32.200 --> 00:31:38.320
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Is there anything else you want to tell me about how you're doing?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>还有什么你想告诉我的关于你近况的事情吗？

00:31:38.320 --> 00:31:40.580
<v Banias>I'm already so sleepy.
<v Banias>我已经很困了。

00:31:40.580 --> 00:31:47.020
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yeah, it's late. So I hope you have an easy night, Banias.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>好吧，天色很晚了。希望你有个安稳的夜晚，Banias。

00:31:47.020 --> 00:31:54.940
<v Banias>I hope so.
<v Banias>希望如此。

00:31:54.940 --> 00:32:15.820
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>An incomplete list of things Banias does not have control over-- can she go home? No. Is there food? Not enough. Is there school? No. Is there safety here? No. Banias lives in what has become the most dangerous place in the world to be a child.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Banias 无法掌控的事情清单不完全统计——她能回家吗？不能。有食物吗？不够。有学校吗？没有。这里安全吗？没有。Banias 生活在目前世界上对孩子来说最危险的地方。

00:32:15.820 --> 00:32:44.580
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Disease in Gaza is widespread. Children face acute malnutrition. Kids are getting horrible skin infections. Polio has reappeared in a 10-month-old baby. Children are losing their limbs, their parents, and they are being killed, constantly. More than 13,000 children have been killed so far, including at least 710 babies, some of them born and then killed since the war began.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>加沙的疾病十分普遍。孩子们面临严重营养不良。孩子们患上了可怕的皮肤感染。小儿麻痹症在一名 10 个月大的婴儿身上复现了。孩子们正在失去四肢、失去父母，而且他们不断被杀害。到目前为止，超过 13,000 名儿童被杀害，其中包括至少 710 名婴儿，有些婴儿从战争开始就出生然后被杀。

00:32:44.580 --> 00:33:00.070
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Maram told me Banias has seen dead children. She's seen their small bodies wrapped in white cloth by the hospital. I asked Maram later, what do you think Banias gets out of talking to me? She told me, you're a bubble for her.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Maram 告诉我 Banias 见过死去的孩子。她见过医院里用白布包裹着的小尸体。我后来问 Maram，你觉得 Banias 从与我的通话中得到了什么？她告诉我，你对她来说是一个气泡。

00:33:00.070 --> 00:33:14.890
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Every time you call, she treats it like an important meeting, tries to find a private space away from all of us. Everyone around Banias is in the midst of this chaos, she said. You're not here. You're not experiencing any of this.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>每次你打电话，她都把它当作一次重要的会议，试图找一个远离我们所有人的私密空间。她说，Banias 周围的每个人都身处这片混乱之中。你不在现场。你没有经历这一切。

00:33:14.890 --> 00:33:41.440
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Banias was telling me a version of life where she has ultimate authority, where she gets to be the narrator. Who doesn't want that? I was coming to her to understand the war, but she was coming to me to not talk about the war, until one day, she did. That's coming up from Chicago Public Radio, when our program continues.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Banias 正在向我讲述一个拥有绝对主权的生活版本，在那里她是叙述者。谁不想要那样呢？我通过她去理解战争，而她通过我来逃避谈论战争，直到有一天，她不得不谈起。这就是我们要带来的内容，来自芝加哥公共广播电台，我们的节目稍后继续。

00:33:41.440 --> 00:33:52.510
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>It's This American Life. I'm Chana Joffe-Walt, sitting in for Ira Glass. Our show today, "The Narrator," an eight-year-old in Gaza, tells us about her life in the middle of a war.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>这里是《美国生活》。我是 Chana Joffe-Walt，代替 Ira Glass 主持节目。我们今天的节目《叙述者》，加沙的一名八岁孩子，讲述了她在战争中的生活。

00:33:52.510 --> 00:34:14.370
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>This war started in 2023. Hamas attacked Israel, killed about 1,200 people, and took 251 people hostage. Since then, Israel has launched a 14-month ground invasion and bombing campaign in Gaza. More than 44,000 Palestinians have been killed, and more than 13,000 of those dead are children.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>这场战争始于 2023 年。哈马斯袭击了以色列，杀害了约 1,200 人，并劫持了 251 人为人质。从那时起，以色列在加沙发动了为期 14 个月的地面入侵和轰炸行动。超过 44,000 名巴勒斯坦人被杀，其中超过 13,000 名死者是儿童。

00:34:14.370 --> 00:34:40.890
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Banias and her family never moved into a tent. After the Israeli army issued that evacuation order for Deir Balah, her parents agonized over when and if they should flee for days. The dangers of moving into a tent could be worse than tanks outside their house. They decided to stay put. It was early October. The family was coming up on a year of war and displacement, and Banias had an announcement.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Banias 和她的家人从未住进帐篷。在以军针对代尔拜拉赫发布疏散令后，她的父母挣扎了几天，考虑是否以及何时应该逃离。搬进帐篷的危险可能比房屋外的坦克还要严重。他们决定留在原地。那是十月初。这家人即将度过一年的战争与流离失所，而 Banias 有一个重大宣布。

00:34:40.890 --> 00:34:49.230
<v Banias>The war stopped. The war stopped. Do you know, the war stopped?
<v Banias>战争停止了。战争停止了。你知道吗，战争停止了？

00:34:49.230 --> 00:34:53.110
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yesterday, there was no bombing or fighting?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>昨天没有轰炸或战斗了吗？

00:34:53.110 --> 00:34:59.170
<v Banias>No. Ever, never. The war stopped.
<v Banias>没有。永远，从来没有。战争停止了。

00:34:59.170 --> 00:35:00.740
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What are you talking about?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你在说什么？

00:35:00.740 --> 00:35:06.340
<v Banias>Because our house was bombed.
<v Banias>因为我们的房子被炸了。

00:35:06.340 --> 00:35:09.040
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Your house was bombed?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你们房子被炸了？

00:35:09.040 --> 00:35:11.490
<v Banias>Yeah. Just kidding.
<v Banias>是啊。开玩笑的。

00:35:11.490 --> 00:35:11.890
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>[LAUGHS]
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>[笑]

00:35:11.890 --> 00:35:12.790
<v Banias>But--
<v Banias>但——

00:35:12.790 --> 00:35:15.160
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What are you doing to me, Banias?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你这是在对我做什么，Banias？

00:35:15.160 --> 00:35:27.620
<v Banias>But there was good news yesterday. Yesterday, tonight, it was-- wee! We had a party. There was very, very good news.
<v Banias>但昨天有好消息。昨天，今晚，那是——呜！我们举行了派对。那是非常、非常好的消息。

00:35:27.620 --> 00:35:30.580
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What was the good news?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>什么好消息？

00:35:30.580 --> 00:35:39.010
<v Banias>Oh. Um-- we have killed all of them.
<v Banias>哦。嗯——我们杀了他们所有人。

00:35:39.010 --> 00:35:44.050
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What do you mean? Who did you kill all of?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你是什么意思？你杀了谁的全部？

00:35:44.050 --> 00:35:54.260
<v Banias>Not all of them-- thousands and thousands and thousands of them! But I can't remember who.
<v Banias>不是所有人——成千上万，成千上万的人！但我记不清是谁了。

00:35:54.260 --> 00:35:57.140
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>You're talking about the Israelis?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你说的是以色列人？

00:35:57.140 --> 00:36:03.290
<v Banias>Yes, yes. Thousands and thousands. We killed thousands, thousands, thousands.
<v Banias>是的，是的。成千上万。我们杀了成千上万，成千上万。

00:36:03.290 --> 00:36:12.090
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>I realized as we were talking, this was October 2. The day before, Iran had launched 180 missiles at Israel.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>谈话中我意识到，那天是 10 月 2 日。前一天，伊朗向以色列发射了 180 枚导弹。

00:36:12.090 --> 00:36:12.780
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>That was--
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>那是——

00:36:12.780 --> 00:36:24.170
<v Banias>Yes, that was yesterday. Yesterday, we had a party for that. We bring coffee, make juice. Oh! Kay-yef-nah.
<v Banias>是的，那是昨天。昨天，我们为此举行了派对。我们拿来咖啡，榨果汁。哦！Kay-yef-nah。

00:36:24.170 --> 00:36:25.670
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Kay-yef-nah?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Kay-yef-nah？

00:36:25.670 --> 00:36:26.300
<v Banias>Yes.
<v Banias>是的。

00:36:26.300 --> 00:36:28.940
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What's "kay-yef-nah" mean?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>“Kay-yef-nah”是什么意思？

00:36:28.940 --> 00:36:33.890
<v Banias>That means "we had a good time" in Arabic.
<v Banias>那在阿拉伯语里意思是“我们玩得很开心”。

00:36:33.890 --> 00:36:38.600
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Banias, you're talking about the missiles yesterday to the Israelis?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Banias，你在谈论昨天针对以色列人的导弹？

00:36:38.600 --> 00:36:39.920
<v Banias>Yes.
<v Banias>是的。

00:36:39.920 --> 00:36:42.630
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>How did you feel about that?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你对此有什么感觉？

00:36:42.630 --> 00:36:51.930
<v Banias>It was-- whoa! It was very good. [NON-ENGLISH]
<v Banias>那是——哇！非常好。[非英语]

00:36:51.930 --> 00:37:13.620
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>This threw me, hearing Banias talk about killing Israelis. No Israelis were killed from these missiles. One Palestinian man was, near Jericho. It's one of those empty truisms about war, that kids in a war learn to hate the other side, a true thing about war that also can feel a little abstract.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>听到 Banias 谈论杀害以色列人让我感到震惊。这些导弹并没有炸死任何以色列人。有一名巴勒斯坦男子在杰里科附近遇难。关于战争的一个陈词滥调是，战区的孩子学会仇恨另一方，这是一个关于战争的真实事实，但有时听起来可能有点抽象。

00:37:13.620 --> 00:37:35.310
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>But here it was, showing up, randomly folded into the rest of Banias's narration to her playing with me, messing with me, that the home she was sheltering in was bombed-- which it could have been, but wasn't. I asked Maram if I could talk with her about this day. I told her what Banias had told me.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>但它确实出现了，随机地交织在 Banias 对我的叙述中，跟我玩闹、跟我开玩笑说她居住的房子被炸了——虽然那本可能发生，但实际上没有。我问 Maram 我能否和她谈谈这一天。我告诉了她 Banias 跟我说的话。

00:37:35.310 --> 00:37:37.380
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What was happening that day?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>那天发生了什么？

00:37:37.380 --> 00:37:59.260
<v Maram Hamaid>Yeah, actually, on that day, it was a huge surprise, actually. Suddenly, we were at home, and we heard the sounds of cheer and people around us cheering and chanting. The internet was cut.
<v Maram Hamaid>是的，实际上那天是一个巨大的惊喜。我们当时在家里，突然听到欢呼声，周围的人在欢呼雀跃。互联网断了。

00:37:59.260 --> 00:38:29.290
<v Maram Hamaid>And I thought from the first instance that there was a ceasefire or something like this. The war ended, you know? So people around us started to say that Iran is bombing Israel right now. And we could see the lights of the missiles being sent to Israel, in the sky. And people around us are just cheering and celebrating and clapping.
<v Maram Hamaid>起初我以为是停火之类的。战争结束了，你知道吗？周围的人开始说伊朗现在正在轰炸以色列。我们能看到导弹射向以色列的火光，就在天空中。周围的人只是在欢呼、庆祝和鼓掌。

00:38:29.290 --> 00:38:51.490
<v Maram Hamaid>I was in emotion. I was very emotional. I really cried. I felt like, oh, my God, really? Someone who's trying just to stop Israel, and to say that by the missiles and by the rockets, the same language that Israel understands and uses in Gaza throughout the years.
<v Maram Hamaid>我当时情绪很激动。我真的哭了。我感觉，哦，天哪，真的吗？有人正在试图阻止以色列，并说通过导弹和火箭，用以色列多年来在加沙理解和使用的同一种语言。

00:38:51.490 --> 00:38:55.800
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Were you celebrating? Were you guys celebrating?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你在庆祝吗？你们在庆祝吗？

00:38:55.800 --> 00:39:10.170
<v Maram Hamaid>I didn't. We were just like excited. We stayed home because maybe missiles could drop by mistake on us. We were just trying to follow up the news.
<v Maram Hamaid>我没有。我们只是很兴奋。我们留在家里，因为导弹可能会错误地掉在我们头上。我们只是试着追踪新闻。

00:39:10.170 --> 00:39:27.540
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Maram told me she does not tell Banias to hate Israel or celebrate when Israel is attacked. Banias's dad, she says, also doesn't do this. But Maram was not surprised to hear Banias was saying this. She remembers feeling the same way when she was a kid growing up in Gaza.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Maram 告诉我，她没有教 Banias 去仇恨以色列或在以色列被攻击时庆祝。她说 Banias 的爸爸也不会这样做。但 Maram 并不惊讶听到 Banias 会这么说。她记得自己还是个在加沙长大的孩子时，也有过同样的感觉。

00:39:27.540 --> 00:39:52.390
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Maram was 10 years old when she first experienced Israeli bombing after the Second Intifada broke out. She remembers crying when she saw her first dead body and collapsing when she saw footage of a 12-year-old Palestinian kid, Mohammed al-Durrah, killed while hiding next to his father. Banias was born in 2016. Her first war was when she was four years old.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Maram 10 岁时第一次在第二次大起义爆发后经历了以色列的轰炸。她记得第一次看到尸体时大哭，看到 12 岁的巴勒斯坦孩子穆罕默德·杜拉在父亲旁边躲藏时被杀的录像时崩溃。Banias 出生于 2016 年。她的第一次战争是在四岁时。

00:39:52.390 --> 00:40:20.830
<v Maram Hamaid>I totally understand that she herself, as a Palestinian kid, she views Israel as an enemy, an enemy that bombs us, that kills us, that targets us.
<v Maram Hamaid>我完全理解她自己作为一名巴勒斯坦孩子，将以色列视为敌人，一个轰炸我们、杀害我们、针对我们的敌人。

00:40:20.830 --> 00:40:43.390
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>There's something I've been thinking about when it comes to kids in wars, but kids in Gaza in particular. It's something a psychologist told me, Dr. Iman Farajallah, who studies the effect of war and occupation on Palestinian kids. She told me it really gets under her skin when people at the UN or healthcare professionals or whatever say kids in Gaza are suffering from PTSD.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>关于战区的孩子，特别是加沙的孩子，我一直在思考一件事。心理学家 Iman Farajallah 博士告诉过我，她研究战争和占领对巴勒斯坦孩子的影响。她说，当联合国的人、医护人员或其他什么人说加沙的孩子患有 PTSD（创伤后应激障碍）时，她非常反感。

00:40:43.390 --> 00:41:15.350
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Post-traumatic stress means the traumatic event is over. For kids in Gaza, the trauma is continuous. There is no post. There's no opportunity for recovery. Instead, there is just coping. Dr. Farajallah says, you'll see kids cope in all different ways. Some kids act out. Some can't leave their parents' side. Other kids get obsessed with soccer or drawing. Or children try to shape their world in other ways.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>“创伤后”意味着创伤事件已经结束。对于加沙的孩子来说，创伤是持续的。没有所谓的“后”。没有恢复的机会。相反，只有应对。Farajallah 博士说，你会看到孩子们用各种不同的方式应对。有的孩子行为反常。有的不能离开父母一步。其他孩子沉迷于足球或绘画。或者孩子们试图用其他方式塑造他们的世界。

00:41:15.350 --> 00:41:36.120
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>For instance, Maram told me when Banias was six years old, there was an Israeli military operation in Gaza, lots of fighting. And Banias was sitting on the window, watching ambulances rush people to the hospital, blowing bubbles out the window. Maram asked her, what are you doing? And Banias said, I'm trying to change the mood.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>例如，Maram 告诉我，Banias 六岁时，以色列在加沙进行了一次军事行动，有很多战斗。Banias 当时坐在窗边，看着救护车把人送往医院，对着窗外吹泡泡。Maram 问她，你在做什么？Banias 说，我在尝试改变心情。

