00:47:38.510 --> 00:48:00.770
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Any war is a series of plot points. Even in an ongoing war, a never-ending and no-longer-new war, we track its progress by the worst moments. I kept calling Banias with this expectation, waiting for the story of the war as I was understanding it, to somehow intersect with her life as she was experiencing it.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>任何战争都是一系列的情节点。即使是在一场持续的、无休止且不再新鲜的战争中，我们也通过最糟糕的时刻追踪它的进展。我一直在怀着这种期望给 Banias 打电话，等待着战争的故事——就像我所理解的那样——以某种方式与她所经历的生活交叉。

00:48:00.770 --> 00:48:13.040
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>I kept imagining, dreading, that one of those moments will break through, that something bad will happen to Banias. One of those horrible plot points will become her plot point.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我不断想象，甚至恐惧，那其中的一个时刻会突破防线，Banias 会发生不好的事。那些可怕的情节点之一会成为她的情节点。

00:48:13.040 --> 00:48:31.160
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>But something bad is happening to Banias. This is the plot point for her. She's sitting under the covers with no electricity, no heat, winter approaching. Banias has not been in school for over a year. She has no home. She has a cough, and there is no medicine.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>但坏事确实正在发生在 Banias 身上。这就是她的情节点。她躲在没有电、没有暖气的被子里，冬天即将来临。Banias 已经一年多没有上学了。她没有家。她咳嗽，没有药。

00:48:31.160 --> 00:48:48.940
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Her friends have scattered. Some of them are dead. Her relatives are all over. Some of them are dead. She's eating canned beans, instead of burgers. She's finding glass in her brother's head. This is her life. This is the story she has to narrate.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她的朋友们四散奔逃。其中一些已经死了。她的亲戚遍布各处。一些也死了。她吃着罐装豆子，而不是汉堡。她在弟弟的头上发现玻璃碎片。这就是她的生活。这就是她必须叙述的故事。

