00:49:03.490 --> 00:49:11.120
<v Banias>Oh? Do you want to leave? I want to continue this movie and then go to sleep.
<v Banias>哦？你想离开了吗？我想看完这部电影然后睡觉。

00:49:11.120 --> 00:49:14.470
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>OK, sleep well. I'll talk to you soon.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>好的，晚安。我们很快再聊。

00:49:14.470 --> 00:49:16.940
<v Banias>Where are you? Are you still here?
<v Banias>你在哪？你还在吗？

00:49:16.940 --> 00:49:17.660
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>I'm here.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我在。

00:49:17.660 --> 00:49:20.360
<v Banias>Hello? Hello?
<v Banias>喂？喂？

00:49:20.360 --> 00:49:21.020
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>I'm here.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我在。

00:49:21.020 --> 00:49:21.800
<v Banias>Are you still here?
<v Banias>你还在吗？

00:49:21.800 --> 00:49:32.390
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yes, I am.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>是的，我在。

00:49:32.390 --> 00:49:57.600
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>We have a couple minutes left in this episode, and I have a small update. Recently, Banias's family moved-- not far-- an apartment a couple miles from Deir Balah, where they've been staying. The new place is less crowded. There's more privacy for her family. It has trees outside and a refrigerator-- that doesn't work, but still. The apartment is quiet, temporary.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>这一集节目还剩下几分钟，我有一个简短的更新。最近，Banias 的一家搬了家——离得不远——搬到了代尔拜拉赫几英里外的一处公寓。新地方没那么拥挤。她的家人有了更多的隐私。外面有树，还有一个冰箱——虽然不能用，但还是有的。公寓很安静，是暂时的。

00:49:57.600 --> 00:50:17.480
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And it's not home. Banias knows she can't go home to the north of Gaza, where she's from. She knows her home was destroyed. She's seen pictures of her neighborhood exploded, on fire. And she's seen video of the empty space where her house was, the small mountains of rubble.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>那不是家。Banias 知道她回不去加沙北部了，那是她的家乡。她知道她的家被毁了。她看过照片，她附近的社区被炸毁、起火了。她看过视频，那是她家曾经所在的地方，成了一座小小的瓦砾山。

00:50:17.480 --> 00:50:42.870
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>The gray couch with yellow cushions that she sat on after school, the chandelier her mother chose, the mirror by the door, the teacups and trays filled with treats, her new reimagined big girl bedroom with an Elsa bedspread, her desk, the pink moon they hung on the ceiling-- all of that is somewhere in that pile of rubble. All of that is there in the north of Gaza, their life.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她放学后坐的黄色坐垫灰色沙发、她母亲挑选的吊灯、门口的镜子、装满点心的茶杯和托盘、她那间重新装扮的拥有 Elsa 床单的大女孩卧室、她的书桌、他们挂在天花板上的粉色月亮——所有这些都在那堆瓦砾里的某个地方。所有这些都在加沙北部，他们的生活。

00:50:42.870 --> 00:51:06.270
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>But the north of Gaza has been transformed. There were about a million people living in northern Gaza when the war started, over 270,000 homes. Everyone was told to leave, to go south. Most people did. And now those people are separated from the north of Gaza by a wide militarized zone that they cannot cross.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>但加沙北部已经变样了。战争开始时，约有一百万人住在加沙北部，有超过 27 万户房屋。每个人都被告知离开，去南部。大多数人照做了。而现在，这些人被一个宽阔的军事化区域与加沙北部隔开，他们无法穿越。

00:51:06.270 --> 00:51:35.780
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Israel has been building and fortifying this military zone for the last few months. It cuts right across Gaza, splits Gaza in two, completely separating the north of Gaza, where Banias is from, from the south of Gaza, where she's been displaced to. This military zone is called the Netzarim Corridor. It has a constant military presence, and it's big, around 20 square miles. It takes up more than 12% of the entire territory of Gaza.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>以色列过去几个月一直在建造和加固这个军事区域。它直接穿过加沙，将加沙一分为二，完全将 Banias 来自的加沙北部与她被流离失所到的南部隔开。这个军事区域被称为“内扎里姆走廊”（Netzarim Corridor）。它有常驻的军事存在，而且规模很大，约有 20 平方英里。它占据了整个加沙地带超过 12% 的面积。

00:51:35.780 --> 00:51:57.200
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>In order to build it, Israel cleared out a wide stretch of land, demolished hundreds of buildings, from the Israeli border all the way to the ocean. And in that space, Israel installed checkpoints and paved roads and flags and water lines and cell phone towers. It looks like something you'd put in place if you're planning to stay a while.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>为了建造它，以色列清理了一大片土地，拆毁了数百座建筑，从以色列边境一直延伸到海洋。在这个空间里，以色列安装了检查站、铺设了道路、插上了旗帜、铺设了水管和手机信号塔。它看起来像是如果你计划留在这里一段时间会做的事情。

00:51:57.200 --> 00:52:17.150
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>A former chief of staff of the Israeli military has called the emptying out of the north of Gaza an ethnic cleansing. He said, quote, "the land is being cleared of Arabs." Human Rights Watch, Oxfam, Amnesty International have all called what is happening in Gaza an ethnic cleansing, or a genocide.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>一位以色列军方前参谋长称加沙北部的清空行动为“种族清洗”。他说，引用，“土地正在被清理，没有阿拉伯人。”人权观察、乐施会、国际特赦组织都称加沙正在发生的事情为种族清洗或种族灭绝。

00:52:17.150 --> 00:52:34.260
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Israel denies this, and the Israeli military sent me a statement calling the charge of ethnic cleansing entirely baseless. It says it's working to dismantle Hamas's military infrastructure and is adhering to its obligations under international law.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>以色列否认了这一点，以色列军方给我发了一份声明，称种族清洗的指控完全毫无根据。声明称，它正在致力于拆除哈马斯的军事基础设施，并遵守其在国际法下的义务。

00:52:34.260 --> 00:52:49.830
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>The people who remained in the north and never left are under siege, with increasingly limited food and medical care. The UN says children are, quote, "as ever, the first and most to suffer."
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>留在北部没走的人正处于围困之中，食物和医疗护理日益匮乏。联合国表示，儿童是“一如既往，首当其冲且受害最深的人”。

00:52:49.830 --> 00:53:33.220
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>So this latest move for Banias's parents, it feels like a new phase. It's a move from "I can't believe it's gone on this long" to "this is going to keep going on." For Banias, it's more of the same, more temporary, more displacement, displacement that looks pretty likely to last most, if not all, of her childhood.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>所以对于 Banias 的父母来说，这次最新的搬迁感觉像是一个新阶段。这是一个从“不敢相信这会持续这么久”到“这会一直持续下去”的转变。对于 Banias 来说，这更多的是一样的东西，更多的临时性，更多的流离失所——这种流离失所看起来极有可能持续她童年的大部分甚至全部时光。

00:53:33.220 --> 00:53:54.800
